  "summary": "The giant shark Otodus megalodon, found in seas almost worldwide, vanished from the fossil record in the Pliocene. A 2019 reassessment of its youngest reliable fossils put the extinction near 3.6 million years ago (median estimate 3.51 Ma), earlier than a previous Pliocene-Pleistocene estimate of 2.6 Ma.",
